+- **`lrtest(..., test = :bootstrap)` adds a parametric bootstrap null (#1116, #1118).** It simulates from the reduced fit, refits both models on the supplied `data`, and returns `pvalue`, `nsim`, `seed`, and `failed`. The default packaged p-value stays naive χ² (#304). The 50:50 chi-bar mixture from `lrt_boundary` is conservative with few groups: type-I at α = 0.05 is at most 5% with no lower bound. t10 recorded 3.0% and 3.4%; those rates are expected. Twin of drmTMB `anova(..., test = "bootstrap")`.
