+# After Task: parametric bootstrap null for lrtest (#1116, #1118)
+
+## Goal
+
+Give an applied user a finite-sample p-value for a boundary likelihood-ratio
+test without changing the packaged default. Shinichi chose, on 16 Oct 2026
+at 5:23 PM MT, to keep the 50:50 chi-bar mixture as the default reference
+and add a parametric bootstrap under the null as an option. This is the
+Julia twin of drmTMB FX6b.
+
+## Implemented
+
+`lrtest(reduced, full; test = :bootstrap, nsim, seed, data)` and the
+`anova` alias simulate new responses from the reduced fit, refit both
+models on the supplied `data`, and return `pvalue`, `nsim`, `seed`, and
+`failed`. The p-value is the Davison–Hinkley count
+`(1 + #{T* ≥ T_obs}) / (1 + n_ok)`. `data` is required because a
+`DrmFit` does not retain its table.
+
+The default packaged p-value stays naive χ² (#304). The 50:50 chi-bar
+mixture from `lrt_boundary` is documented as conservative with few
+groups: type-I at α = 0.05 is at most 5% with no lower bound. t10
+recorded 3.0% (NB2 vs Poisson) and 3.4% (`(1 | g)`); those rates are
+expected.
+
+## Files Changed
+
+`src/comparison.jl`, `test/test_bootstrap_lrt.jl`, `NEWS.md`, this
+report.
+
+## Checks Run
+
+`julia --project=.` on pin `f71b292` plus the FX6 warning patch and this
+change: `test/test_bootstrap_lrt.jl` and `test/test_family_boundary_lrt.jl`.
+
+## Next Actions
+
+Push to `itchyshin/DRModels.jl` if write access exists; otherwise keep
+the twin as a patch on the drmTMB side.
